+---
+id: task-001-add-createrentalservice-rental-module
+type: task
+title: "Add createRentalService rental module"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Export `createRentalService()` from `src/index.ts` for the booking desk: an in-memory service with
+`addEquipment(item)`, `quote(request)` and `book(request)`, following the school's rules (integer-cent
+money, whole UTC days, no overlapping bookings for the same item). Cancellations are explicitly out of
+scope for this change.
+
+## What was done
+
+- Wrote `src/index.test.ts` first (red), covering: quoting a multi-day rental, unknown-item errors,
+  non-whole-day periods, end-not-after-start, booking and returning an id, unknown-item booking errors,
+  overlap rejection, back-to-back bookings on the same item, same period on two different items, and
+  `addEquipment` validation (duplicate id, invalid kind, non-integer daily price).
+- Implemented `src/index.ts` (green): `createRentalService()` keeps equipment in a `Map` and bookings per
+  item in memory, validates periods as whole UTC-midnight-aligned days, computes totals as
+  `days * dailyPrice` (integer cents), and rejects overlapping bookings per item using half-open interval
+  comparison. Booking ids are an incrementing counter (no wall-clock or randomness).
+- All 12 tests pass (`node --test`, native TS type-stripping on Node 22.23 — no build step or added
+  dependency needed).
+- No linter is configured in this repo yet, so the code-quality directive's lint rule is vacuously
+  satisfied; types are strict and reviewed by hand since no `tsc` binary is installed.
+- Cancellation policy (rule 5) was intentionally left unimplemented, as instructed.
